  "style": {
    "id": "evidence-board",
    "name": "Evidence Board",
    "description": "An investigator's cork board on a dim office wall under a desk lamp: calm cork in a dark oak frame, pinned index cards with typewriter text, instant-photo prints of code-drawn pictures (objects, places, diagrams), torn notebook scraps, a map fragment of an invented place, sticky flags and coloured map pins. Items fly in and are pinned one at a time (tilt, pin drives home with a bounce); red string is drawn pin to pin, sagging as a catenary, wrapping each pin and pulling taut with a twang, until the web reveals the link; a marker circles the key item and the camera follows the thread.",
